# profiles/qwen27b.env -- Qwen3.8-27B (NVFP4), the local_llm CLI's "inline"
# backend. Replaces ~/Projects/local_llm/bin/qwen-server-run.sh, which is the
# ExecStart of the qwen-vllm.service user unit and the script
# bin/soak-27b-overnight.sh drives.
#
# TWO THINGS HERE ARE LOAD-BEARING AND MUST NOT BE "TIDIED":
#  1. P_READS_CONFIG=1 -- $CONFIG_FILE is SOURCED AFTER these defaults, so a
#     value in .config beats both the default and the caller's environment.
#     bin/soak-27b-overnight.sh depends on exactly that: it writes a frozen
#     .config.27b-soak and hands it over as CONFIG_FILE so a concurrent switch
#     of the live .config to Flash-Next cannot steer the soak onto the wrong
#     model, port, or -- worst -- util 0.95.
#  2. P_EXEC=1 -- the launcher execs vLLM so systemd's main PID is the real
#     server, its SIGTERM reaches vLLM directly, and ExecStopPost
#     (bin/qwen-server-record-death.sh) still fires on every exit.
P_FAMILY=qwen27b
P_ROOT="$HOME/Projects/local_llm"
# vLLM 0.29.0 (.venv-llm-029) since 2026-09-11, carrying the is_left_overlap
# fix from PR #50729 for the GDN/Mamba state-copy race. 0.27.1 (.venv-llm) at
# util 0.95 died twice on 2026-09-11 (18:16:56 Xid 31; 19:26:27 SIGSEGV in
# CUDAGraph::replay). .venv-llm stays on disk as the rollback; pass
# VLLM_VENV=.../.venv-llm to use it, and do not run it at 0.95. Must match
# VLLM_VENV's default in bin/qwen-server-run.sh and servedeck.toml's
# [backends.inline] venv.
P_VENV="$HOME/Projects/local_llm/.venv-llm-029"
P_CONFIG_DEFAULT="$HOME/Projects/local_llm/.config"
P_READS_CONFIG=1

P_MODEL="RadixArk/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4"
# 8004, not 8000: 8000 is permanently held by the unrelated, autostarting
# ats-optimizer.service.
P_PORT=8004
# 0.47 is the value the Aug 2026 crash bisection settled on after Xid 13/31 hit
# at util=.62 and util=.92. It has run Xid-free for 9+ real days. The
# 2026-09-09 re-test of .62 did NOT reproduce the fault, but only in ~11-15 min
# windows, so it is not evidence. Do not raise it without a multi-hour soak.
P_GPU_UTIL=0.47
P_MAX_LEN=262144
P_MAX_SEQS=128
P_FLASHINFER_SAMPLER=0

# Written with the interior spaces the old script used, because the golden test
# compares this argument byte for byte.
P_SPEC_JSON='{"method": "mtp", "num_speculative_tokens": 4}'
P_TOOL_PARSER=qwen3_xml
P_REASONING_PARSER=qwen3

# Guards. The VRAM guard asks "is there room for us" (util x total + margin),
# not "is anyone else on the card" -- a fixed 8 GB trip-wire refused to start
# three times on 2026-08-22 while 70 GB were free. Exit 69 = EX_UNAVAILABLE,
# which qwen-vllm.service treats as a stand-down (RestartPreventExitStatus=69)
# rather than a crash to restart into.
P_GUARD_TRAINING_MARKER=1
P_TRAINING_MARKERS="$HOME/Projects/local_llm/run/training_in_progress $HOME/.cache/algotrading/training_in_progress /home/pctablet505/Projects/AlgoTrading/run/training_in_progress"
P_GUARD_VRAM=1
P_GPU_HEADROOM_MIB=4096
P_SWEEP_ORPHAN_ENGINECORE=1

# One timestamped log per run plus a stable symlink, keeping the newest 10. The
# pre-2026-08-22 launcher truncated a single file on every start, which is why
# the 2026-08-21 23:24 crash left no log at all.
P_LOG_MODE=rotate
P_LOG_STEM=qwen_server
P_LOG_SYMLINK=qwen_server.log
P_LOG_KEEP=10
P_DEATH_LOG="$HOME/Projects/local_llm/logs/qwen_deaths.log"
P_EXEC=1

# P_ENV_KNOBS: the optional environment knobs the script this profile
# replaces actually honoured. Anything not listed is ignored, so the
# unified launcher cannot accept a knob the old path did not.
P_ENV_KNOBS=""

# P_DEATH_HOOK fires from the launcher's own cleanup() and therefore ONLY on
# the non-exec path. With P_EXEC=1 (above) systemd is the supervisor and
# qwen-vllm.service's ExecStopPost runs this same script, so the hook is inert
# today and cannot double-record. It is set so that flipping P_EXEC to 0 --
# e.g. to run the 27B outside systemd -- does not silently lose the death log
# that exists because a vLLM whose engine dies exits with status 0.
P_DEATH_HOOK="$HOME/Projects/local_llm/bin/qwen-server-record-death.sh"
